 Because `frai-core` is a regular ESM package, you can import only the modules you need and embed FRAI capabilities inside automation pipelines, CI jobs, or custom products.
 
+Example: evaluate model outputs with metric thresholds.
+
+```js
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const dataset = Eval.loadDataset({
+  outputsPath: './outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: './references.json'
+});
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({
+  outputs: dataset.outputs,
+  references: dataset.references
+});
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: dataset.outputsPath,
+  referencesPath: dataset.referencesPath,
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    length_variance: 0.85
+  }
+});
+
+const resolvedPath = Eval.writeReport({
+  report,
+  format: 'json',
+  reportPath: './report.json'
+});
+
+if (report.passed === false) {
+  console.error('Thresholds failed.');
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
+The `thresholds` parameter accepts an object mapping metric IDs to minimum scores (0–1). The report includes a `passed` field and a `thresholds` list showing which thresholds passed or failed. This works with the default metrics and custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`.
+
 ---
 
